      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "The sattvic relinquisher, pervaded by sattva, does not hate unpleasant action and does not cling to pleasant action; he is wise and has cut through doubt. Śrīdhara gives difficult cold-water bathing as an example of unpleasant duty and pleasant bathing as an example of pleasant duty.",
